  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Female Judges Training in MENA Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This tailor-made &#x201c;Access to Justice &#x2013; Female Judiciary in Yemen and the Middle East and North Africa (MENA) region&#x201d; programme aims to better equip the current and potential female judiciary to navigate the many challenges and gender biases that hinder female professionals in the judiciary in Yemen and the MENA region. The training programme should be designed to help aspiring female professionals develop the critical leadership skills to influence, persuade, empower, and mentor other women. Those preparing to transition into more senior roles will be able to deepen their leadership knowledge by reflecting on crucible moments and approaches to challenging situations.The training programme should serve those aiming to overcome gender barriers in the judiciary, and grow both within their careers and organisation. Next to leadership skills, the training will also focus on enhancing the participant&#x2019;s knowledge on Dutch and international judicial processes and procedures which should in turn help to inspire and apply lessons learnt in their own contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
